---
title: Citrus Chicken and Quinoa Stir-Fry
course: main
cuisine: asian
servings: 4
time_active: 25
time_total: 35
leftovers: good
tags: [weeknight]
---

Rinse @quinoa{3/4%cup} and combine with @chicken broth{1 1/2%cups}(low-sodium) and a pinch of salt in a #saucepan{}. Bring to a boil, then cover and simmer until absorbed, ~{12-15%minutes}. Fluff and spread on a plate to cool.

Slice @chicken breast{1%lb}(boneless, skinless) into 1/4-inch strips and season with @salt{1/4%tsp} and @black pepper{1/8%tsp}.

== Citrus Glaze ==

Whisk @soy sauce{2%tbsp}(low-sodium), the juice of @orange{1}(large, about 1/4 cup), @chicken broth{1/4%cup}, @honey{1%tbsp}, and @cornstarch{1%tsp}.

== Stir-Fry ==

Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a #large skillet{} over medium-high. Stir-fry the chicken with @garlic{1%clove}(minced) and @?fresh ginger{1%tsp}(grated) until cooked through, ~{5-6%minutes}. Move to a plate.

In the same pan, stir-fry @red bell pepper{1}(thinly sliced) and @sugar snap peas{1%cup}(trimmed) until crisp-tender, ~{2-3%minutes}. Stir the glaze, add it, and cook until thickened, ~{1-2%minutes}.

Return the chicken, add the quinoa, and toss in the glaze ~{1%minute}. Off the heat, fold in @arugula{2%cups} until just wilted. Season to taste.

Garnish with @?scallions{2%tbsp}(chopped, or cilantro) and @?toasted sesame seeds{1%tsp}, and serve with @?lime{1}(cut into wedges).

> Partly freezing the chicken makes it easier to slice thin. Leftovers keep 2 days; reheat with a splash of broth.
